> Prepare fitting, validation and test pixels through the native API

`prepare_example_data("mnist-assets",...)` creates the canonical saliency pools:
1000 fitting,200 validation and200 test rows. `LoadSaliency` retains labels and
source IDs, with unit-range Float32 pixels. `BigGanResize8` performs the source's
28-to-8 half-pixel bilinear resize: Double coordinates and four-term accumulation
followed by one Float32 cast. Labels identify the preview rows only; the GAN is
unconditional and never consumes labels. Every pool and its original28x28 values,
labels and source IDs are saved in data.npz.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/progressive_pools.png", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
  namespace n     = dm::nn;
  const auto path = std::filesystem::path(dm::datasets::data_home()) / "saliency";
  dm::datasets::prepare_example_data("mnist-assets", path.parent_path());
  auto                      pools  = n::models::LoadSaliency(path);
  auto                      labels = pools[0].labels.to_vector<std::int64_t>();
  std::vector<std::int64_t> rows;
  for (int c = 0; c < 10; ++c) {
    int found = 0;
    for (std::size_t i = 0; i < labels.size() && found < 2; ++i)
      if (labels[i] == c) {
        rows.push_back(i);
        ++found;
      }
  }
  n::save_image_grid(
      n::take_rows(n::models::BigGanResize8(pools[0].images), rows),
      "build/progressive_pools.png",
      2,
      0,
      1,
      4,
      220 / 255.,
      8);
  std::print("Fit/validation/test rows:1000/200/200; preview shows two fit examples per digit.\n");
}
```
